# Python libraries

Before designing or reviewing a reusable infrastructure helper or its caller, match the need
below and read its design rule. Read the implementation template only when adding, adapting,
or reviewing the helper itself. Use only rows whose design rule is installed in the target
repository.

| Need | Existing helper | Design | Implementation |
|---|---|---|---|
| Finite persisted lifecycle with a meaningful transition graph | `StateMachine` / `AsyncStateMachine` | [`python-fsm.mdc`](../python-fsm/python-fsm.mdc) | [`FSM.md`](FSM.md) |
| Smallest independently repeatable transient adapter operation; idempotent writes and per-attempt timeout | `retry_on_exception` / `retry_unless_exception` | [`python-retry.mdc`](../python-retry/python-retry.mdc) | [`RETRY.md`](RETRY.md) |
| Outbound HTTP adapter using the developer-selected async or sync client | `AsyncApi` / `SyncApi` | [`python-base-client.mdc`](../python-base-client/python-base-client.mdc) | [`ASYNC_CLIENT.md`](ASYNC_CLIENT.md) or [`SYNC_CLIENT.md`](SYNC_CLIENT.md) |
| OpenAI speech-to-text or text-to-speech through the existing LLM client | `stt` / `tts` | this rule | [`SPEECH.md`](SPEECH.md) |
| Operator CRUD UI over SQLAlchemy ORM models | sqladmin `Admin` / `ModelView` | [`python-sqladmin.mdc`](python-sqladmin.mdc) | upstream package `sqladmin[auth]` |
| Rate limiting inbound FastAPI routes (Redis-backed) | fastapi-limiter `RateLimiter` | [`python-fastapi-limiter.mdc`](python-fastapi-limiter.mdc) | upstream package `fastapi-limiter` |
| User JWT authentication on FastAPI routes | PyJWT + pwdlib in `libs/security.py` | [`python-jwt.mdc`](python-jwt.mdc) | [`SECURITY.md`](SECURITY.md) |

Use ordinary conditionals for independent flags or lifecycles without a meaningful transition
graph.

## Speech

Dependencies: `openai`, `pydub`, and system `ffmpeg` (`uv add openai pydub`).
Render [`SPEECH.md`](SPEECH.md) into `project/infrastructure/adapters/speech.py`
(copy only if missing).
- Telegram voice messages: download as bytes (`download_as_bytearray()`),
  pass `bytes` to `stt`.
